Chapter: UnitFieldAccess
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Field access through a unit wrapper is refused at CHECK.

 Until 2026-07-28 the checker ACCEPTED this. The receiver fell through
 the field-access arms to the fresh-type-variable fallback, so `s.x`
 was given an unconstrained type and the compile ran on to emit, where
 it died with `CDX2000: emit-field-access: unresolved type for field
 'x'` -- a message about the emitter's internals, at a phase the author
 has no reason to be reading, for a mistake the type system can see.

 The fallback it fell through is load-bearing for genuine inference, so
 the fix is this one arm rather than a change to the fallback.

 There is deliberately no unwrap suggested, because there is none. A
 unit over a record cannot be passed where the record is expected
 either: `spot-point : Spot -> Point` taking the identity is CDX2001,
 measured. A unit over a PRIMITIVE is transparent that way and works,
 which is the asymmetry that makes this shape surprising.

Section: Types

  Point = record {
   x : Integer,
   y : Integer
  }

  Spot = unit Point

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let s = Spot (Point { x = 7, y = 9 })
    in print-line-uni ("x=" & show s.x)
  end
